Issue title: argument `num_of_examples` of function `show_batch` is never used

Issue report:
```
https://github.com/tensorflow/models/blame/9a2993d140841f37d73cded94c1295da4faab8b5/docs/vision/instance_segmentation.ipynb#L748
```

Reproduction attempt:
1. Load the `show_batch` cell from `codebase/docs/vision/instance_segmentation.ipynb`.
2. Inspect the function body and confirm `num_of_examples` is never read.
3. Execute `show_batch` with three records and `num_of_examples=1` in a stubbed environment.
4. Observe that the function still processes all three records.

Observed evidence: The notebook helper defines `show_batch(raw_records, num_of_examples)` but never references `num_of_examples`; when called with three records and `num_of_examples=1`, it still renders three subplots.

